# The confession slips: success scene for the writing spot
# (successDialogue). XP and the flag are the comp's job.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_MonConfessions

== start ==
{PLAYER} lifts the top layer of slips and unfolds them one by one.

They are supposed to be confessions of sins. Instead, a dozen different hands across one winter all confess the same thing: I HEAR HUMMING. By the well. On the cellarium stair. In my teeth during prayers.

* [Keep reading.] -> deeper

== deeper ==
None of them told each other. One novice writes: Brother P. hears it too. I watched him stop walking. We did not speak of it.

Every brother thought he was the only one, and the rule kept it that way.

The last slip in the box, in a very neat hand: I no longer hear it. It hears me.

* [Put the slips back the way they were.] -> end
